With approximately 4,787 employees and revenues around $1.4 billion, Eissmann operates production facilities in Europe, North America, Mexico, China, and the United States. Its North American subsidiary, Eissmann Automotive NA, has a significant manufacturing presence in Pell City, Alabama, employing over 800 workers. The company emphasizes quality and process management, adhering to IATF 16949 standards to ensure defect prevention and continuous improvement.

Eissmann serves top automotive manufacturers worldwide, providing high-quality, innovative interior solutions that meet the evolving demands of the industry. The company is committed to delivering functional and exciting car interiors for various vehicle types and drive systems.","updated_at":"2026-08-10T16:36:48.129075Z"}

{"id":"01925571-76c0-7ade-a709-e05a76753dfc","name":"Primus Line","domain":"primusline.com","website":"https://primusline.com","type":"private","legalName":null,"industry":"Construction","industries":["Construction/Civil Engineering Construction","Construction/Architecture, Engineering & Design"],"categories":["b2b","service-provider"],"employees":"11-50","reported_employees":"201-500","revenue":null,"description":"Primus Line provides trenchless rehabilitation solutions for pressurized pipelines and overland piping, focusing on safe, reliable, and sustainable restoration of water, gas, and oil networks. Manufactured in Germany and deployed worldwide, the Primus Line system uses a flexible liner and connectors to rehabilitate existing pipelines without excavation, enabling efficient project delivery with reduced environmental impact. The company emphasizes high quality, emissions-conscious methods and operates as part of the Werner Rädlinger group.","keywords":["trenchless rehabilitation","pressure pipeline relining","kevlar reinforced liner","flexible pipe technology","overland piping","water pipeline rehabilitation","gas pipeline rehabilitation","oil pipeline rehabilitation","pipeline liner","relining of pipelines","emissions reduction in pipeline repair","safe pipeline rehabilitation","sustainable infrastructure","underground pipe rehabilitation","in-situ pipe rehabilitation","polymer liner systems","ductile pipe rehab","underground retrofit","industrial piping restoration","pipeline rehabilitation","trenchless technology","flexible pipes","water transport","oil transport","gas transport","infrastructure solutions","construction"],"technologies":["Cloudflare DNS","Microsoft Office 365","CloudFlare Hosting","Remote","Outlook","Cloudflare-Cdn","Google-Tag-Manager","Matomo","Nginx","Php","Plesk","Typo3-Cms"],"subsidiaries":null,"founded_year":2001,"naics_codes":["237120","237990","541330"],"location":{"country":{"code":"US","name":"United States","latitude":38,"longitude":-97},"state":{"id":4881,"name":"North Carolina","code":"NC","latitude":35.759575,"longitude":-79.0193},"city":{"id":141726,"name":"Charlotte","latitude":35.22709,"longitude":-80.84313},"address":"112 South Tryon Street, Suite 1130 Charlotte, NC 28284-2109 United States of America","postal_code":"93413","phone":"+1 704 5694460"},"financial":{"stock_symbol":null,"stock_exchange":null,"total_funding":null,"funding_stage":null,"funding_date":null,"funding":null},"socials":{"linkedin_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/r-dlinger-primus-line-gmbh","linkedin_id":"3015869","twitter_url":null,"facebook_url":"https://www.facebook.com/primusline/","instagram_url":null,"angellist_url":null,"crunchbase_url":null,"youtube_url":"https://www.youtube.com/@RaedlingerPrimusLine","github_url":null,"g2_url":null},"page_rank":2.4291048,"logo_url":"https://api.companyenrich.com/companies/logo/01925571-76c0-7ade-a709-e05a76753dfc","seo_description":"Rädlinger Primus Line GmbH is a German company that specializes in trenchless rehabilitation solutions for pressure pipelines. Established in 2001 as a subsidiary of the Rädlinger Group, the company has over 20 years of experience in flexible fabric reinforced pipe (FFRP) technology. It combines expertise from construction, mechanical engineering, and web technology to create advanced pipeline rehabilitation systems.

The company's main product is the Primus Line® system, a flexible, Kevlar®-reinforced liner designed for the trenchless rehabilitation of pressure pipes used in water, gas, and oil applications. This system features specially developed end fittings and is known for its flexibility, lightweight design, and strength comparable to steel pipes. Rädlinger Primus Line serves a diverse range of customers, including waterworks, network operators, and oil companies, and has successfully completed projects across multiple continents.

The company prioritizes safety, reliability, and sustainability in its operations. With international subsidiaries and logistics centers, Rädlinger Primus Line is committed to expanding its global presence while delivering high-quality solutions for pressure pipe renovation.","updated_at":"2026-08-15T07:09:33.650065Z"}

